# Playback meaningful events

Use one rule everywhere: **the audio advanced, or the user acted on it.**

## Meaningful vs non-meaningful

| Meaningful                            | Not meaningful                                |
| ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Play pressed                          | App opened                                    |
| Pause pressed                         | Item hydrated from the server                 |
| Seek, scrub, skip-back-15             | Screen rendered or navigated to               |
| Timer tick while actively playing     | Background refresh or sync pull               |
| Track completed or auto-advanced      | Position write while paused (nothing changed) |
| Skip to next or previous              | Queue list merely displayed                   |
| Sleep timer stopping playback         |                                               |
| Queue item added, removed, reordered  |                                               |

## Why exclusions are load-bearing

App open, hydration, and passive refresh must not bump playback recency. If they did, a stale
offline device could overwrite newer listening from another device without any real playback action.

## Why inclusions are load-bearing

Long listening sessions need timer ticks while playing to keep recency accurate. Without them, a
session can hold an old timestamp and lose merges to unrelated touches from another device.

## Shared check only

Use `isMeaningfulPlaybackEvent` from `@podverse/helpers` everywhere. Do not duplicate this check in
app-local helper logic.

## Zone move vs removal tombstone

| User action                     | Event kind     | Emits a tombstone? |
| ------------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------ |
| Plays a queued item             | `play`         | No                 |
| Queued item finishes            | `complete`     | No                 |
| Skips past a queued item        | `skip`         | No                 |
| Deliberate queue delete action  | `queue_remove` | Yes                |

## Handoff behavior guardrails

Same-item now-playing disagreements adopt the newer position silently. Do not add a prompt,
threshold, or position-delta rule for that case.

Only different-item disagreements ask the user to choose, and reconciliation must never load a
different item while playback is active locally.
